cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Qimen Dunjia symbolic features versus seasonal baselines for CPC daily precipitation occurrence"
message: >-
  If you use these analysis artifacts, cite this repository and the NOAA CPC
  precipitation product. The manuscripts in manuscript/ are unpublished drafts.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Haopeng
    alias: 李浩鹏
    affiliation: City University Malaysia
repository-code: "https://github.com/Gideon-li/qimen-precip-analysis"
url: "https://github.com/Gideon-li/qimen-precip-analysis"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-07"
keywords:
  - NOAA CPC
  - precipitation occurrence
  - Brier score
  - Qimen Dunjia
  - seasonal baseline
abstract: >-
  Scored outputs and documentation for one computational experiment.
  Thirty-one noon Qimen Dunjia symbolic features are compared with seasonal
  baselines and other models on 267 cells of the NOAA CPC Global Unified
  Gauge-Based Analysis of Daily Precipitation (V1.0), retrieved through
  NOAA PSL NCSS. Train 2023, validation 2024, test 2025. On the 2025 test,
  a per-cell season-only L2 logistic model has Brier score 0.1923 and the
  Qimen-plus-season model has Brier score 0.1970 (delta +0.0047; circular
  10-day block bootstrap, 400 draws, 95 percent interval +0.0033 to +0.0061).
  The sample is a 2-degree lattice near project administrative centroids,
  not a national census and not China Meteorological Administration station
  data. No human-affairs outcome is evaluated.
